Replace the fixed pipeline with a deepagents orchestrator on hosted Nemotron

The seven-node LangGraph pipeline ran each node once, so it could call cuOpt
exactly one time and had no way to react to the answer. Slotting is not a
one-shot problem: the first solve is what reveals which constraint actually
binds. The sequence is now the model's to choose.

Models
  Both Nemotron models run on NVIDIA's hosted endpoint. The self-hosted
  Lightning NIM cannot run on these B300s -- its vLLM build does not recognise
  the card's native FP4 support, falls back to Marlin kernels and the engine
  core dies after loading the weights. cuOpt is now the only thing needing a
  GPU, so the job asks for one instead of four.

  deepagents ships a tuned harness profile for Nemotron 3 Ultra, but it is
  registered against model specs that all spell the model
  nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b. Our hosted endpoint answers to
  nvidia/nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra, which matches none of them, so the harness
  silently resolved an empty profile and dropped all twelve middleware and the
  2962-character prompt suffix. services/harness_profile.py re-registers the
  shipped profile under the spec our client reports, and raises the progress
  budget, which at 3 repeated tool calls would have aborted the re-solve loop.

Orchestrator
  agents/deep_workflow.py reads measured state, delegates to three specialists,
  solves, inspects what the solve would actually buy, and solves again while
  addressable headroom remains. It picks the move count and the solver budget
  inside the operator's cap; the cap itself stays human-set. create_approval
  names the round it recommends, because the run that chose a smaller round and
  silently filed the larger one gave the operator a plan the narrative did not
  describe. A later approval retires the earlier one for the same reason.

  showcase/kpis.py gains project_moves(), which shows what a solve would do
  without committing it. That projection is what makes the loop possible.

Analysis
  showcase/analysis.py replaces detect_problems(). A threshold cannot tell a
  genuinely bad layout from one already optimal for its demand, and has no idea
  the move cap puts most remaining headroom out of reach. The model is given the
  measured facts and judges; the arithmetic stays in code.

Deployment
  Several teammates share a node and run this same stack, so ports move to a
  private 28xxx block, state and logs become per-user, and the app is handed its
  URLs as process environment. Without that, skip_if_up saw a teammate's healthy
  service and wired our app to their containers.
